  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/... \nEnsemble guidance favors some weakening of the subtropical high\nstarting Friday as it starts to shift back to the east. This shift\nassumes a Pacific trough moving into the Northwestern U.S. late\nweek. Models also favor some gradual moisture advection by Friday\nand lasting through the upcoming weekend. Given the expected \nincrease in moisture and weakening subsidence, rain chances should\nreturn as early as Friday but more likely over the weekend. \nNBM/WPC PoPs show 10-15% chances over high terrain areas Friday \nand Saturday before increasing and expanding into the lower \ndeserts by Sunday. These PoPs may be underdone somewhat \nconsidering what the latest models runs show, so we anticipate \nhigher PoPs soon from the NBM. Temperatures should also begin to \nimprove late week and through the weekend as moisture increases \nand heights gradually lower. The latest forecast highs still \nmaintain or even top 110 degrees through Saturday before dropping \nto below 110 degrees by Sunday or Monday of next week.",
